15. Defense Pitfalls
Many SSRF protections fail due to incorrect assumptions.
Common mistakes:
Blocking only localhost
Developers block:

127.0.0.1
But forget:

10.0.0.0/8
192.168.0.0/16
169.254.0.0/16


Checking URL before DNS resolution
Example vulnerable flow:

Validate URL → Resolve DNS → Send request
Attackers exploit this using DNS rebinding.
Correct flow:

Resolve DNS → Validate IP → Send request


Trusting redirects
Example:

allowed-domain.com → redirect → internal IP
Applications must revalidate redirect targets.


